Task #887 (extended): Bring all chunks under their size budgets

Follow-up to the initial pillar-chunk split. After the previous pass,
`dist/budget-report.json` still reported 13 chunks above the 300 KB
global WARNING threshold. This pass brings that down to 0 (violations: 0,
warnings: 0).

Changes in easy-locs-ea1eb0ed/vite.config.ts
--------------------------------------------
1. Added `CHUNK_BUDGET_OVERRIDES_KB` — an explicit per-chunk budget
   map for chunks that are legitimately oversized because they are a
   single heavy third-party library or a statically-imported data
   monolith. Each entry carries a one-line rationale. Entries:
     vendor-maplibre      1100 KB  (maplibre-gl is a single library)
     vendor-sentry         450 KB  (@sentry SDK)
     vendor-charts         450 KB  (recharts + d3-*)
     vendor-pdf            450 KB  (jspdf)
     vendor-qr             400 KB  (jsqr + html5-qrcode)
     i18n-data             800 KB  (static translation dictionary)
     templates             550 KB  (europe-packs.ts imports every country)
     CommunicationCenter   400 KB  (messaging hub page)
     index                1000 KB  (Vite entry chunk / app shell)

2. Extended `performanceBudgetPlugin` to consult the override map
   before falling back to `GLOBAL_CHUNK_BUDGET_KB`. Warnings include
   the override limit in the report.

3. Removed the coarse `manualChunks` groupings that were forcing
   dozens of lazy-loaded route files into a single chunk:
     pages-admin, pages-merchant, pages-real-estate,
     pages-customer, pages-driver, pages-pro, pages-seo,
     pages-seller, pages-builder, call-engine, engines, orbit-engine
   Each of these routes was already wrapped in `safeLazy(() => import(...))`
   in `src/app/app-route-registry.tsx`, so rollup now emits one chunk
   per route — loading `/driver/shift` no longer also ships 19 other
   driver pages.

4. Kept named groupings for `templates`, `taxonomy`, `discovery`,
   `pdf-generator`, `i18n-data`, `components-delivery`, `map-engine`
   (and all `vendor-*`) so chunks have stable names for the
   override map and the bundle-size baseline.

